{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/447568-about-serving-judges","id":447568,"title":"About Serving Judges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-18T05:11:42-07:00","id":447568,"title":"About Serving Judges","content":"This might sound like an odd question. On the book it's said that a mummy serves it's judge which basically is his master. Anyway when a mummy is awakened, most of the time it's to help his cultists. So what's exactly the meaning of &quot;Serving his own Judge&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T05:58:00-07:00","id":447599,"title":"","content":"Collecting relics, destroying Amkhata and other Lifeless abominations, glorifying Irem, the Shaniatu, and the Judges, saving the life of another Arisen (especially one that serves the same Judge as you), punishing your Judge's chosen sinners, correcting heretics, obeying the odd instincts that sometimes come into your head while in henet. These are all things that (probably) please the Judges. They're more than a little inscrutable, so it's always kind of a mystery what does and doesn't please them until you actually do something and find your Descent either reset or forced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:16:24-07:00","id":447897,"title":"","content":"Also, keep in mind that each of the judges enjoys punishing a certain type of sinner (&quot;sinner&quot; in the context of a set of morality that was ancient at the time of Cleopatra). The judges certainly like it when the Arisen inflict their type of justice to sinners of their purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T17:22:42-07:00","id":448517,"title":"","content":"It's actually intriguingly ambiguous, since a Cultist can raise an Arisen for seemingly any purpose and yet the Judge will punish them for not following their Purpose. Even if said Purpose directly contravenes what seems to be the Judge's own goals (commit sins or help those that the Judge itself punishes, aid the Shuankhsen, pursue Apotheosis).<br /> <br /> To me, it brings three things to mind. The first is the whole &quot;Mysterious ways&quot; argument, in that Fate ensures that the Arisen's Purpose will be aligned to that of the Judges, even if it seemingly does not. The second is, interestingly enough, the possibility that the &quot;Judges&quot;, if that's what they actually are, are almost non-sentient and incapable of acting outside of the... &quot;programming&quot; built into the Rite of Return. They can't do much more than provide rewards in certain listed situations and check to see if Arisen are following their Purpose. If yes, reward. If no, punish. Their actual ability to pass judgement on the purpose itself is so limited to be non-existent.<br /> <br /> The third is that the Book of Going Westward would be really, really useful if it clarified some of this stuff. Or a supplement on Arisen cults and any direct connection they may have to their master's Judge. Or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T04:06:29-07:00","id":448991,"title":"","content":"I think some more information on the Judges is the main thing missing now. The Deceived are really interesting because they have this dynamic of having such a close relationship with their masters, but by their very nature the Arisen aren't as close with those distant overlords. Still, I wonder how the <b>Book of Going Westward</b> would expand that relationship into something just as engaging as the temakhs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T11:56:02-07:00","id":449558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/447568-about-serving-judges?p=448991#post448991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think some more information on the Judges is the main thing missing now. The Deceived are really interesting because they have this dynamic of having such a close relationship with their masters, but by their very nature the Arisen aren't as close with those distant overlords. Still, I wonder how the <b>Book of Going Westward</b> would expand that relationship into something just as engaging as the temakhs</div> </div> </div> </div>Still trying to bang my head around the Temakhs in general. The Deceived in general are horrifying unto themselves but the Temakhs themselves seem to lack an overall plan of action vs &quot;Just burn all civilization down!&quot;.<br /> <br /> In which you burn it all down and then what? Your soul fragments are still stuck in the bodies of the Deceived.<br /> <br /> You have eternity to plan and execute those plans. You were once masters of Sekhem and wielded power unfathomable and yet you spent all your time and energy collecting relics and the like. <br /> <br /> Really tempted to create a Movement which is less about collecting Relics and is more about rebuilding their own Irem &quot;with hookers and blackjack&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also tempted to make a Movement which is focused on the Deceived focusing on human experimentation with Sekhem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T13:00:56-07:00","id":449642,"title":"","content":"Tearing it all down isn't about personal gain, it's about making others lose. It's vengeance and pettiness writ on a cosmic scale. But there are competing impulses at play. How can there be more art on which to feed and collect seba from without artists, and how can there be artists without civilization? It isn't so much that the temakhs lack a plan so much as they are pulled in so many directions by not really knowing what they want most. Above all, remember that they are insane: truly, absolutely, and terrifyingly. They don't have to make sense. They ARE, and just by being, they are a strange and in some ways unknowable plague upon the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T13:58:49-07:00","id":449746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/447568-about-serving-judges?p=449642#post449642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tearing it all down isn't about personal gain, it's about making others lose. It's vengeance and pettiness writ on a cosmic scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable and is one of the reasons why I pity their human hosts so much.<br /> <br /> Think of a True Fae. Now remove all the quirky personality. Now take a Seer of the Throne and strip away all pretenses of Virtue. Blend well and you have the petulant outlook of the Temakhs.<br /> <br /> For all their power, for all their cults and abilities. For all their cries of former Godhood, I find the Temakhs simply pathetic in terms of outlook.<br /> <br /> They got themselves into their own mess. They're clearly not rational about long term goals, and they spend so much time focused on back stabbing each other over Seba that it hampers any progress that they make on them.<br /> <br /> They've gotten themselves into a hole with being attached to their human hosts and yet instead of trying to climb out of it, they engage in behavior that is no way productive to their current state.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 03-19-2015, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:07:57-07:00","id":449755,"title":"","content":"Pathetic Godmonsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T19:58:05-07:00","id":450035,"title":"","content":"That's really the beauty of this antagonist: that they were once so much and could be so much if they chose, but that they prefer the petty vengeance you'd expect of a child despite being 10,000 year old god-spirits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T21:07:52-07:00","id":451274,"title":"","content":"To be fair(er than they deserve) they aren't exactly lucid. Their minds are split across all their mummies, and they don't ever get all together to think about things. Their base desires absent broader context are almost the only thing that could survive in that state so as to influence their hosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}